  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing the impact of Ukraine electricity supply-demand gap through demand side management.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programme would aim to strengthen Ukraine#s demand side management/demand response (DSM/DR) programmes by working with Ukraine T ransmission System Operator (UKRENERGO) and relevant Oblenergos, the regional Ukrainian Distribution System Operators (DSOs), and an initial sizeable pool of large and medium-size industrial and critical infrastructure electricity consumers to enhance Ukrainian power grid flexibility, load factor and efficiency; and to incentivize end-user energy efficiency.  The Programme would combine procurement of equipment for power grid management and for energy/power management within consumers# facilities with the provision of DSM/ DR expertise and capacity building to personnel of UKRENERGO and Ukrainian DSOs on the one hand, and expertise and capacity building on energy management, energy efficiency &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; energy demand forecasting to personnel of industrial and other facilities participating in the DSM/ DR programmes.  Immediate benefits of UNIDO#s interventions would be to support Ukraine in: 1. Reducing number, extension (in terms of customers affected) and duration of planned &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; unplanned black-outs experienced by Ukraine population and businesses as Ukraine#s power/energy generating capacity is rebuilt 2. Reducing industrial and other big consumers# power demand and energy con</narrative>
  </description>
